  "description": "NAMHIV crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H88 Er6 N10 O32. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er1D (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2D (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3D (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.512-3.953 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.64-113.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C78H88Er6N10O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
